{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvaePhwepFG6gGFQQ9XA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't approve the six-week study as proposed. Reshape it into a capped, conditional step.**\n\n**Why**\n- The bank has made on-prem a requirement but won't commit to a timeline or volume. You would be paying real cost for an unpriced option.\n- No other customer has asked for on-prem. A feasibility study for one prospect can easily turn into a product-direction decision, with ongoing support and release burden, that no one has made deliberately.\n- Legal added the requirement late. It may be a template clause that the bank would drop for a private-cloud or single-tenant option. It may also be a quiet way to slow the deal. You don't know which, and that is the first thing to find out.\n\n**What to do instead**\n1. **Clarify first (days, not weeks).** Ask the bank, through sales, what exactly they require. Is it on-prem, or is it data residency, customer-managed keys, or a dedicated VPC? Ask who owns the requirement and whether a sponsor will back it.\n2. **Cap the engineering.** Give one engineer about one week for a desk assessment. They should list which components assume your hosted environment and give a rough order-of-magnitude effort. They shouldn't build or prototype anything.\n3. **Ask for something in return** before any deeper work. A signed LOI, a paid proof of concept, or a stated minimum volume would all count. If the bank won't give any of these, that tells you how real the demand is.\n4. **Set a kill criterion.** If the requirement is truly hard on-prem and the bank still won't commit, park the deal and say so plainly.\n\n**Decision rule:** invest more only when the bank's commitment is in writing and large enough to cover the support cost of a second deployment model."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3848,"cache_read_input_tokens":4609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3848},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18084bd8-ac6c-41b5-a60b-aeeb9f5bdfc7","uuid":"eda2d45e-42cb-42fa-81ec-3de20b531bcc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:08:17.209Z","request_id":"req_011CfvaePUJofHSKG1KpvXxd"}
